    "/api/v1/rl/checkpoints/{name}/weights": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "rl",
          "rl"
        ],
        "summary": "Get Checkpoint Weights",
        "description": "Export a saved PPO checkpoint as JSON-serializable weights.\n\nThe frontend uses this to instantiate an in-browser MlpPolicy for\nreplay (see `src/infrastructure/rl/mlpInference.ts`). Returns the\npolicy `state_dict()` flattened to nested lists + architecture\nmetadata (`obs_dim`, `action_dim`, `hidden_sizes`).\n\nDeliberately a **sync** endpoint: the export loads a PPO checkpoint\n(cold: seconds), and FastAPI runs sync endpoints in the threadpool.\nAs an `async def` it would block the whole event loop for the\nduration of the load, stalling every other request.\n\nThe export itself is memoised per checkpoint file by\n`app.apps.rl.weights.export_weights`, so only the first request per\ncheckpoint pays the load cost.\n\nErrors:\n  - 404: checkpoint file not found\n  - 503: SB3 / torch not installed (run `uv sync --extra rl`)",
        "operationId": "get_checkpoint_weights_api_v1_rl_checkpoints__name__weights_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "name",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "title": "Name"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "additionalProperties": true,
                  "title": "Response Get Checkpoint Weights Api V1 Rl Checkpoints  Name  Weights Get"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
